                <pb facs="0857" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-15T23:00:00-05:00">December 15, 1928—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 16—5:04 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>143. Your 87, December 14, 6 p.m. Today I saw President Leguia. The President
                    agrees with you that the authorities of Chile would probably find out about
                    Colonel Moore’s visit and the reasons therefor. Since he does not wish anyone to
                    know what is in his mind, <pb facs="0858" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/> and he has
                    not even told one of his Ministers, he has decided not to send Colonel Moore. I
                    will keep you informed of any later developments. President Leguia may send
                    someone else.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
